    "turn_idx": 49,
    "turn_text": "Well, it clearly indicates that we do have a very important role of the United States in the world promoting freedom and democracy, American values. And we also have such a record of success. We've gone over it. Whether you begin with the Marshall Plan, go through Plan Colombia, you go to the restoration of freedom and democracy in Korea, the recovery that we made for that country to become one of the world's most significant and successful economic stories. There's not a place that you can't go where you've seen, I think, a positive American influence in Kenya. Very important in Africa, what we've done with the relationships there. And also Ethiopia. And also very significant last year was in Tunisia. to see the success of that country over and over again in North Africa. And Morocco, what a success story working with the United States. And one of my favorites is actually Mongolia. Meeting with government officials there, they said, hey, Congressman, we love America. You're part of our three-legged stool. And we would fall over. We have good relationship with the Russian Federation, good federate, good relationship with the People's Republic, and best relationship with the United States of America. And that's why we're free.",
